  "Question": "A line segment parallel to the vertical axis has length 8. What length should it have in an oblique dimetric drawing?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "With the recorded interpretation of “vertical axis” as the original planar \\(y\\)-axis of a horizontally placed figure, a parallel line segment is drawn at half its original length. Its drawn length is therefore \\(8/2=4\\).\n\nThis interpretation matters: an upright spatial axis keeps its full length in the usual school spatial extension, which would give \\(8\\). Thus the answer \\(4\\) depends on the recorded planar-axis interpretation.",
